    "risk_summary": "Known Cr–Re σ competition and a PBE study finding no ordered stable binary compound are contrary priors, not a transfer of their phase energetics to this NC/PBEsol C15 state. Exact C15 magnetism and the experimental realization of this ordered composition remain unknown.",
    "ambient_scope": "Exact model force/full stress, converged electronic outputs, reported finite-q workflow and raw Γ optical evidence provide a bounded near-ambient source-model screen. Source residual stress/metastable alternatives remain explicit; this is not proof of synthesizeability, full BZ or global equilibrium.",
    "route_response": "C15 A versus tetragonal B supplies a genuine different species network: mean Cr–Cr distance 2.34856 versus 2.44756 Å. λ favors A across all ten rows, and Eliashberg improves by 7.416 K; fine F is lower for A by 15.86 meV/atom. Complete species-channel geometry differences and computed all-σ pairing response are saved against the frozen controls. Cell/grid/method sensitivity prevents a pure geometry-only causal claim; no bandwidth/carrier quantity is substituted.",
    "next_action": "Use C15 exact-state spin seeds and the closest σ ordering as the discriminating competitor, keeping the same phase-specific EPC control. A magnetic C15 phase that suppresses the benefit reverses the present nonmagnetic hypothesis.",
    "seven_criteria": {
      "identity": "Source-specific full-species CIF→both SCF inputs→Γ coordinate/cell association, actual atom order and origin, within 1e-6 Å observational matching policy. Original experimental occupancy and measured P/T unknown; configured QE neutral/nonmagnetic/no-SOC model is distinct from a magnetic ground-state claim.",
      "novelty": "One exact reduced composition/ordered phase-design group, new to the frozen reviewed cohort. Published computed source is acknowledged, known experimental chemistry remains a comparator. Bounded primary phase search has not tied the exact target order to an established SC sample; no global absence claim.",
      "quantitative_route_response": "C15 A versus tetragonal B supplies a genuine different species network: mean Cr–Cr distance 2.34856 versus 2.44756 Å. λ favors A across all ten rows, and Eliashberg improves by 7.416 K; fine F is lower for A by 15.86 meV/atom. Complete species-channel geometry differences and computed all-σ pairing response are saved against the frozen controls. Cell/grid/method sensitivity prevents a pure geometry-only causal claim; no bandwidth/carrier quantity is substituted.",
      "pairing_relevance": "All ten source λ/ω rows retained with original units/nulls, and μ*=0.1 source McMillan, Allen–Dynes and Eliashberg products kept separate. Source Gaussian EPC broadening is distinct from explicit MP electronic SCF smearing. No product maximum or selected σ defines the recommendation.",
      "ambient_feasibility": "Exact model force/full stress, converged electronic outputs, reported finite-q workflow and raw Γ optical evidence provide a bounded near-ambient source-model screen. Source residual stress/metastable alternatives remain explicit; this is not proof of synthesizeability, full BZ or global equilibrium.",
